      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T19:31:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That bug is assuming a specific use-case that doesn\u0027t apply fully in all the factory conditions. If one wants to apply this because of certain platform factory conditions it should be configurable -- not hard coded policy that would apply to everyone. The examples I gave are realistic in the reef/coral platform as well as octopus if model_id and oem_id were employed.\n\nYes, I\u0027m saying board version stays. Other fields go or are configurable to be included in this check. We need flexibility, and this hard-coded policy has larger implications on the factory side of things if cbi were used and these fields were deployed in reef/coral/octopus.",
